# Introduction

Court Archive is a Shopify practice store built around basketball training, recovery, and lifestyle products. The store is designed for athletes who treat basketball as more than a hobby and want products that fit both their training routine and everyday lifestyle. This report reviews checkout-related settings and presents the policies and trust signals that would help customers feel more comfortable shopping online. Because this is a classroom practice store, no real payments or transactions were activated or processed.

# Checkout Review Evidence

I reviewed the checkout-related areas in Shopify, including checkout settings, payment options, shipping and delivery settings, and customer information requirements. I confirmed where a real retailer would connect a payment provider, choose the information collected during checkout, configure shipping rates, and manage delivery or pickup options. I did not activate a real payment method or place a real order.

