# Privacy and Customer Data Statement

## Court Archive Privacy Statement

Court Archive would collect only the information needed to operate the online store, such as a customer's name, email address, shipping address, billing information, order details, and messages submitted through the contact form. This information would be used to process orders, provide customer service, prevent fraud, communicate order updates, and improve the website experience.

Customer information would not be sold. Information may be shared only with service providers needed to operate the store, such as Shopify, payment processors, shipping carriers, analytics providers, or other tools used to complete a transaction. Customers should avoid submitting sensitive personal information through the contact form.

Because Court Archive is a classroom practice store, no real customer payments are being collected. Any future live version of the store should use Shopify's current privacy-policy template and clearly explain cookies, analytics, marketing communication choices, data retention, and customer privacy rights.\
