#  Trust Signals Reflection

Clear policies and store information can make Court Archive feel more professional and reduce the risk customers may feel when shopping from an unfamiliar brand. A customer can review shipping cost and timing before checkout, understand which products may be returned, see how their information would be used, and know how to contact the store if a problem occurs. These details make the buying process more predictable. Trust can be strengthened further by placing links to the shipping, return, privacy, and contact pages in the footer, using consistent branding, showing complete product descriptions and sizing information, displaying secure-checkout messaging, and avoiding surprise charges during checkout.

# CPP Farm Store Application Reflection

The most important trust signals for CPP Farm Store would be accurate product availability, clear pickup instructions, current store hours, the exact pickup location, accepted payment methods, and a dependable way to contact the store. Since many farm products are seasonal or perishable, customers should also know how substitutions, sold-out items, damaged produce, and refund requests are handled. Product descriptions should explain where items come from, how recently availability was updated, and whether refrigeration or quick pickup is recommended. Clear Cal Poly Pomona affiliation, consistent branding, secure checkout information, and visible food-handling or storage guidance would help customers feel confident that the store is legitimate, organized, and prepared to handle their order.

# Conclusion

Reviewing checkout settings showed that customer trust is influenced by more than the products being sold. Customers need to know what will happen during checkout, how and when an order will arrive, what their options are if something goes wrong, how their information is handled, and how to contact the business. Adding these policies and trust signals gives Court Archive a stronger and more complete customer experience while also showing what a real retailer would need before accepting online orders.

